-- Expected values are read off the Act's text and illustrations.  Generated by generators/ea_tests_2.py.

§ `58 to 60. Judicial notice and admitted facts`

`s59 a fact of which notice is taken` MEANS `Judicial Notice Facts` WITH
    `the fact is within section 59(1)(a) to (n)` IS TRUE
    `the fact is a matter of public history, literature, science or art` IS FALSE
    `the person asking the court to take judicial notice produces the book or document the court considers necessary` IS FALSE
    `the parties or their agents agree to admit the fact at the hearing` IS FALSE
    `the parties agree before the hearing, in a writing under their hands, to admit the fact` IS FALSE
    `the parties are by a rule of pleading in force deemed to have admitted the fact by their pleadings` IS FALSE
    `the court requires the admitted fact to be proved otherwise than by the admission` IS FALSE

