§ `61 and 62. Oral evidence must be direct`

`s61 contents of a document` MEANS `Oral Evidence Facts` WITH
    `the evidence is of the contents of a document` IS TRUE
    `the evidence refers to a fact which could be seen` IS FALSE
    `the witness says the witness saw that fact` IS FALSE
    `the evidence refers to a fact which could be heard` IS FALSE
    `the witness says the witness heard that fact` IS FALSE
    `the evidence refers to a fact which could be perceived by another sense or in another manner` IS FALSE
    `the witness says the witness perceived that fact by that sense or in that manner` IS FALSE
    `the evidence refers to an opinion or to the grounds on which it is held` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is that of the person who holds the opinion on those grounds` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is expressed in a treatise commonly offered for sale` IS FALSE
    `the author of the treatise is dead, cannot be found, has become incapable of giving evidence, or cannot be called without an amount of delay or expense the court regards as unreasonable` IS FALSE

`s61 a fact seen` MEANS `Oral Evidence Facts` WITH
    `the evidence is of the contents of a document` IS FALSE
    `the evidence refers to a fact which could be seen` IS FALSE
    `the witness says the witness saw that fact` IS FALSE
    `the evidence refers to a fact which could be heard` IS FALSE
    `the witness says the witness heard that fact` IS FALSE
    `the evidence refers to a fact which could be perceived by another sense or in another manner` IS FALSE
    `the witness says the witness perceived that fact by that sense or in that manner` IS FALSE
    `the evidence refers to an opinion or to the grounds on which it is held` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is that of the person who holds the opinion on those grounds` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is expressed in a treatise commonly offered for sale` IS FALSE
    `the author of the treatise is dead, cannot be found, has become incapable of giving evidence, or cannot be called without an amount of delay or expense the court regards as unreasonable` IS FALSE

