§ `63 to 65. Primary and secondary evidence`

`s64 the document itself` MEANS `Document Facts` WITH
    `the document itself is produced for the inspection of the court` IS TRUE
    `the document was executed in several parts and the thing produced is one of the parts` IS FALSE
    `the document was executed in counterpart and the thing produced is a counterpart offered against a party who executed it` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is one of a number of documents all made by one uniform process, offered as evidence of the contents of another of them` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced and the document it is offered to prove are copies of a common original` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a copy of a document in the form of an electronic record and is shown to reflect that document accurately` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a certified copy given under the provisions of the Act` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a copy made from the original by a technical process that in itself ensures the accuracy of the copy, or a copy compared with such a copy` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a copy made from or compared with the original` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a counterpart offered against a party who did not execute it` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is an oral account of the contents given by a person who has himself or herself seen the document` IS FALSE
    `the original is shown or appears to be in the possession or power of the person against whom the document is sought to be proved` IS FALSE
    `the original is shown or appears to be in the possession or power of a person out of reach of or not subject to the process of the court` IS FALSE
    `the original is shown or appears to be in the possession or power of a person legally bound to produce it` IS FALSE
    `after the notice mentioned in section 68 that person does not produce it` IS FALSE
    `the existence, condition or contents of the original have been proved to be admitted in writing by the person against whom it is proved or by that person's representative in interest` IS FALSE
    `the original has been destroyed or lost` IS FALSE
    `the party offering evidence of its contents cannot, for a reason not arising from the party's own default or neglect, produce it in reasonable time` IS FALSE
    `the original is of such a nature as not to be easily movable` IS FALSE
    `the original is a public document within the meaning of section 76` IS FALSE
    `the original is a document of which a certified copy is permitted by the Act or by another law in force in Singapore to be given in evidence` IS FALSE
