#ASSERT `secondary evidence may be given under section 67(1)(a)` `s67(1)(a) held by the adverse party after notice`

#ASSERT NOT `secondary evidence may be given under section 67(1)(a)` `s67(1)(a) held by the adverse party, no notice`

#ASSERT `secondary evidence may be given under section 67(1)(a)` `s67(1)(a) held by the adverse party, notice dispensed with because it is in court`

#ASSERT `secondary evidence may be given under section 67(1)(a)` `s67(1)(a) held by a person beyond the process of the court`

#ASSERT `secondary evidence may be given under section 67(1)(b)` `s67(1)(b) admitted in writing`

#ASSERT `secondary evidence may be given under section 67(1)(c)` `s67(1)(c) lost`

#ASSERT `secondary evidence may be given under section 67(1)(c)` `s67(1)(c) cannot produce in reasonable time, not by own default`

#ASSERT `secondary evidence may be given under section 67(1)(d)` `s67(1)(d) not easily movable`

#ASSERT `secondary evidence may be given under section 67(1)(e)` `s67(1)(e) a public document`

#ASSERT `secondary evidence may be given under section 67(1)(f)` `s67(1)(f) certified copy permitted by law`

#ASSERT `secondary evidence may be given under section 67(1)(g)` `s67(1)(g) numerous accounts`

#ASSERT NOT `secondary evidence may be given of the document` `s66 no case applies`

#ASSERT `secondary evidence may be given of the document` `s67(1)(b) admitted in writing`

#ASSERT `secondary evidence may be given of the document` `s67(1)(c) lost`

#ASSERT `secondary evidence may be given of the document` `s67(1)(e) a public document`

#ASSERT `secondary evidence may be given of the document` `s67(1)(g) numerous accounts`

#ASSERT `any secondary evidence of the contents is admissible` `s67(1)(c) lost`

#ASSERT `any secondary evidence of the contents is admissible` `s67(1)(d) not easily movable`

#ASSERT NOT `any secondary evidence of the contents is admissible` `s67(1)(b) admitted in writing`

#ASSERT NOT `any secondary evidence of the contents is admissible` `s67(1)(e) a public document`

#ASSERT `the written admission is admissible in proof of the contents` `s67(1)(b) admitted in writing`

#ASSERT NOT `the written admission is admissible in proof of the contents` `s67(1)(c) lost`

#ASSERT `a certified copy is admissible in proof of the contents` `s67(1)(e) a public document`

#ASSERT `a certified copy is admissible in proof of the contents` `s67(1)(f) certified copy permitted by law`

#ASSERT `a certified copy is admissible in proof of the contents` `s67(1)(c) lost`

#ASSERT NOT `a certified copy is admissible in proof of the contents` `s67(1)(g) numerous accounts`

#ASSERT `evidence of the general result by a skilled person is admissible` `s67(1)(g) numerous accounts`

#ASSERT NOT `evidence of the general result by a skilled person is admissible` `s67(1)(e) a public document`

