`s70 attestation required, witness alive, not called` MEANS `Attestation Facts` WITH
    `the document is required by law to be attested` IS TRUE
    `there is an attesting witness alive, subject to the process of the court and capable of giving evidence` IS TRUE
    `at least one attesting witness has been called to prove its execution` IS FALSE
    `no attesting witness can be found` IS FALSE
    `the document purports to have been executed in the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland` IS FALSE
    `it is proved that the attestation of at least one attesting witness is in that witness's handwriting and that the signature of the person executing the document is in that person's handwriting` IS FALSE
    `a party to the attested document has admitted its execution by himself or herself` IS FALSE
    `the attesting witness denies or does not recollect the execution of the document` IS FALSE
    `the signature, writing or seal to be proved is compared with one admitted or proved to the satisfaction of the court to have been written or made by the person it purports to be by` IS FALSE

