#ASSERT NOT `the print may be produced in proof of the contents under section 80A(1)` `s80A a print from a film, document still held`

#ASSERT `the certificate under section 80A(2) is admissible and the court is to presume its contents` `s80A a certificate from a specified body`

#ASSERT NOT `the certificate under section 80A(2) is admissible and the court is to presume its contents` `s80A a certificate from an unspecified body`

§ `67A and 68A`

`s67A the document produced` MEANS `Document Statement Facts` WITH
    `a statement in a document is admissible in evidence by virtue of section 32(1)` IS TRUE
    `the statement is proved by production of the document` IS TRUE
    `the statement is proved by production of a copy of the document, or of the material part of it, authenticated in a manner approved by the court` IS FALSE
    `the materials would be likely to aid the court's comprehension of other evidence that is relevant and admissible` IS FALSE
    `the evidence to be given by a party is so voluminous or complex that the court considers it convenient to assess the evidence by reference to such materials` IS FALSE
    `every fact or opinion asserted in the materials is proved by relevant and admissible evidence, or the party undertakes to prove it and the court is satisfied with the undertaking` IS FALSE

`s67A an authenticated copy of a destroyed document` MEANS `Document Statement Facts` WITH
    `a statement in a document is admissible in evidence by virtue of section 32(1)` IS TRUE
    `the statement is proved by production of the document` IS FALSE
    `the statement is proved by production of a copy of the document, or of the material part of it, authenticated in a manner approved by the court` IS TRUE
    `the materials would be likely to aid the court's comprehension of other evidence that is relevant and admissible` IS FALSE
    `the evidence to be given by a party is so voluminous or complex that the court considers it convenient to assess the evidence by reference to such materials` IS FALSE
    `every fact or opinion asserted in the materials is proved by relevant and admissible evidence, or the party undertakes to prove it and the court is satisfied with the undertaking` IS FALSE

`s67A an unauthenticated copy` MEANS `Document Statement Facts` WITH
    `a statement in a document is admissible in evidence by virtue of section 32(1)` IS TRUE
    `the statement is proved by production of the document` IS FALSE
    `the statement is proved by production of a copy of the document, or of the material part of it, authenticated in a manner approved by the court` IS FALSE
    `the materials would be likely to aid the court's comprehension of other evidence that is relevant and admissible` IS FALSE
    `the evidence to be given by a party is so voluminous or complex that the court considers it convenient to assess the evidence by reference to such materials` IS FALSE
    `every fact or opinion asserted in the materials is proved by relevant and admissible evidence, or the party undertakes to prove it and the court is satisfied with the undertaking` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the statement in the document is properly proved under section 67A` `s67A the document produced`

#ASSERT `the statement in the document is properly proved under section 67A` `s67A an authenticated copy of a destroyed document`

#ASSERT NOT `the statement in the document is properly proved under section 67A` `s67A an unauthenticated copy`

`s68A summaries of voluminous evidence` MEANS `Document Statement Facts` WITH
    `a statement in a document is admissible in evidence by virtue of section 32(1)` IS FALSE
    `the statement is proved by production of the document` IS FALSE
    `the statement is proved by production of a copy of the document, or of the material part of it, authenticated in a manner approved by the court` IS FALSE
    `the materials would be likely to aid the court's comprehension of other evidence that is relevant and admissible` IS TRUE
    `the evidence to be given by a party is so voluminous or complex that the court considers it convenient to assess the evidence by reference to such materials` IS TRUE
    `every fact or opinion asserted in the materials is proved by relevant and admissible evidence, or the party undertakes to prove it and the court is satisfied with the undertaking` IS TRUE

`s68A summaries whose assertions are unproved` MEANS `Document Statement Facts` WITH
    `a statement in a document is admissible in evidence by virtue of section 32(1)` IS FALSE
    `the statement is proved by production of the document` IS FALSE
    `the statement is proved by production of a copy of the document, or of the material part of it, authenticated in a manner approved by the court` IS FALSE
    `the materials would be likely to aid the court's comprehension of other evidence that is relevant and admissible` IS TRUE
    `the evidence to be given by a party is so voluminous or complex that the court considers it convenient to assess the evidence by reference to such materials` IS TRUE
    `every fact or opinion asserted in the materials is proved by relevant and admissible evidence, or the party undertakes to prove it and the court is satisfied with the undertaking` IS FALSE

`s68A summaries of simple evidence` MEANS `Document Statement Facts` WITH
    `a statement in a document is admissible in evidence by virtue of section 32(1)` IS FALSE
    `the statement is proved by production of the document` IS FALSE
    `the statement is proved by production of a copy of the document, or of the material part of it, authenticated in a manner approved by the court` IS FALSE
    `the materials would be likely to aid the court's comprehension of other evidence that is relevant and admissible` IS TRUE
    `the evidence to be given by a party is so voluminous or complex that the court considers it convenient to assess the evidence by reference to such materials` IS FALSE
    `every fact or opinion asserted in the materials is proved by relevant and admissible evidence, or the party undertakes to prove it and the court is satisfied with the undertaking` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `evidence may be given in the form of charts, summaries or other explanatory material` `s68A summaries of voluminous evidence`

#ASSERT NOT `evidence may be given in the form of charts, summaries or other explanatory material` `s68A summaries whose assertions are unproved`

#ASSERT NOT `evidence may be given in the form of charts, summaries or other explanatory material` `s68A summaries of simple evidence`
